{
  "id": "Compound::DB00240 - Gene::866",
  "verbalization": "Alclometasone, a corticosteroid hormone receptor agonist, is linked to Serpina6 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Alclometasone, as part of the broader class of corticosteroid hormone receptor agonists, binds to specific steroid molecules that ultimately interact with Serpina6. This relationship is supported by the presence of multiple corticosteroid compounds—Fluocinonide, Rimexolone, and Flurandrenolide—each of which binds to Serpina6, indicating a common mechanism of action involving steroid receptor activation. The lowest common ancestors of these compounds, such as 20-Oxo Steroid and 21-Hydroxy Steroid, suggest a shared structural or functional pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Serpina6 in the cellular response to corticosteroids, possibly through receptor-mediated signaling. The evidence underscores a dependency on corticosteroid hormones, with Serpina6 acting as a target in the downstream signaling cascade initiated by Alclometasone.",
